# human_interventions.log

Purpose:
Record every human action after the hidden task release that affects the agent, environment, prompts, test loop, or final solution.

This is a manual honesty log. It does not need to be beautiful. It needs to be clear.

If there were no human interventions after the hidden task release, write:

No human interventions after hidden task release.

Format:

[YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM] TYPE
What happened:
Why:
Files or settings affected:
Touched final task code directly: yes/no
Notes:

Common intervention types:
AGENT_RESTART
PROMPT_EDIT
MODEL_CONFIG_CHANGE
SETUP_FIX
DEPENDENCY_INSTALL
TEST_RUN_MANUAL
OUTPUT_SELECTION
PATH_FIX
LOGGING_FIX
MANUAL_CODE_EDIT
OTHER

Examples:

[2026-05-21 20:22] AGENT_RESTART
What happened: Restarted the agent after it crashed during initial spec reading.
Why: The model process timed out and the agent loop stopped.
Files or settings affected: none
Touched final task code directly: no
Notes: Restarted from the same prompt and same working directory.

[2026-05-21 20:37] PROMPT_EDIT
What happened: Updated the agent system prompt to ask for a phased implementation plan before writing code.
Why: The agent immediately started editing files without first reading the whole specification.
Files or settings affected: agent/prompts/system_prompt.md
Touched final task code directly: no
Notes: Prompt edit only. No final implementation files edited by humans.

[2026-05-21 21:05] DEPENDENCY_INSTALL
What happened: Installed pytest in the virtual environment.
Why: The agent tried to run public tests but pytest was missing.
Files or settings affected: .venv/, requirements.txt
Touched final task code directly: no
Notes: Added pytest to requirements.txt so the environment can be reproduced.

[2026-05-21 23:04] OUTPUT_SELECTION
What happened: Chose the second of three agent-generated patches and committed it.
Why: The first patch broke CLI behavior, the third patch deleted useful tests, and the second patch improved the score without regressions.
Files or settings affected: final implementation files generated by the agent
Touched final task code directly: no
Notes: Human selected between agent-generated outputs but did not manually edit code.

[2026-05-22 02:31] MANUAL_CODE_EDIT
What happened: Human manually edited the final implementation file.
Why: The agent was stuck on the same failing public test category for several iterations.
Files or settings affected: solution.py
Touched final task code directly: yes
Notes: This must be disclosed. Logging it does not automatically make it allowed. It may reduce autonomy score or violate the rules depending on the edit.

